<p>The United States and Iran will hold a new round of talks on Tehran’s nuclear programme in Geneva in the coming week. Oman will host the discussions, and Switzerland says it is again offering its “good offices” to help keep the dialogue moving. The meeting follows earlier Oman-mediated talks on Feb. 6 between Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi and U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff, described as indirect discussions with Oman acting as the intermediary. The talks come as Washington pushes for an agreement that would limit Iran’s nuclear activities. The Trump administration has said it wants any deal to include no uranium enrichment—an approach Iran has said it will not accept. Reporting also points to sharper rhetoric and U.S. military signalling in the region alongside the diplomatic track.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4jdgL0aSESH8pgWyKKqkU8GHApLQuiwl9S_C-c_9IGepO6aPP9sz0s3JSImeWyaV0sPbknM55SNvb3QnEvh5vDuDB6pw4ywf7RNL6uObrESe' alt='A staff member removes the Iranian flag from the stage after a group picture during Iran nuclear talks in Vienna on July 14, 2015.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Second-round framing: Swiss authorities called the Geneva meeting a second round of talks on Tehran’s nuclear programme and said it would take place “this week”.</li><li>Feb. 6 participants: Reporting said the Oman talks involved Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi, U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff and President Trump’s son-in-law Jared Kushner, and that Oman mediated the discussions indirectly.</li><li>Trump warning: After the first discussions, Trump warned Tehran that failing to reach an agreement with his administration would be “very traumatic”.</li><li>Pressure signals: Reporting cited Trump saying a change of government in Iran would be the “best thing that could happen,” alongside the U.S. deployment of a second aircraft carrier to the Middle East.</li><li>Military backdrop: Reports also referenced U.S. forces striking Iran’s nuclear programme last July during Israel’s unprecedented 12-day war with Iran.</li></ul><blockquote>Switzerland stands ready at all times to offer its good offices to facilitate dialogue between the United States and Iran - Swiss foreign ministry spokesman</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Swiss Foreign Ministry: Switzerland reiterated its readiness to provide “good offices” and described its protecting-power role, including facilitating minimal diplomatic and consular channels between Washington and Tehran. (<a href='https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/us-iran-hold-new-round-nuclear-talks-geneva-130176100'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: U.S. officials’ stated position is that any agreement must bar Iran from uranium enrichment. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/iran-and-u-s-to-hold-nuclear-talks-in-geneva-swiss-minister-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian government: Tehran’s position, as reported, is that it will not accept a deal requiring it to give up uranium enrichment. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/iran-and-u-s-to-hold-nuclear-talks-in-geneva-swiss-minister-says'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Oman: Oman is described as the host and mediator, including in the earlier indirect talks on Feb. 6. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3343601/us-iran-talks-be-held-geneva-next-week-hosted-oman'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973203/swiss-say-oman-to-host-us-iran-talks-in-geneva-next-week'>Swiss say Oman to host US-Iran talks in Geneva next week</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/us-iran-hold-new-round-nuclear-talks-geneva-130176100'>US, Iran to hold new round of nuclear talks in Geneva this week, Swiss gov. says</a> - abcnews.go.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3343601/us-iran-talks-be-held-geneva-next-week-hosted-oman'>US-Iran talks to be held in Geneva next week, hosted by Oman</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-iran-to-hold-new-round-of-nuclear-talks-in-geneva-this-week-swiss-government-says/article70633413.ece'>U.S., Iran to hold new round of nuclear talks in Geneva this week, Swiss government says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/iran-and-u-s-to-hold-nuclear-talks-in-geneva-swiss-minister-says'>Iran and U.S. to hold nuclear talks in Geneva, Swiss minister says</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>